96	/// Settings view is static — so `updateNSView` rarely fires and AppKit's occasional reset of the
97	/// titlebar/background (on focus changes etc.) would stick, flashing the title bar white. This
98	/// themer instead re-applies on the window's own `didUpdate`/main/key notifications, and guards each
99	/// set so it only writes when something actually reset (no relayout churn). Combined with the
100	/// caller's `.background(tokens.panel.ignoresSafeArea())`, SwiftUI also paints behind the (transparent,
101	/// full-size-content) title bar, so the themed colour holds even between notifications.
